@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ito-il08-nouns`
IMPORT `ito-il08-tax-years`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Income Tax Ordinance s 1, "תושב ישראל" (a) — an Israeli resident, for an individual. Row IL-08.
-- Source lines 143-163.
--
-- GAPS.md item 13 of row IL-07, and row IL-01's coverage table, which left the test out because "the
-- definition is a whole regime of its own". It is encoded here as far as the text decides it, and no
-- further:
--   (1) the centre of life, found on the whole of the family, economic and social ties: an
--       evaluative finding, made by the assessing officer (and on appeal a court), which a
--       determination records. It is an input, NOTHING where none has been made.
--   (2) two presumptions that the centre of life is in Israel, counted in days (part of a day is a
--       day): encoded.
--   (3) either the individual or the assessing officer may rebut them: a presumption decides only
--       where no finding on the ties has been made and it has not been rebutted.
--   (4) regulations of 5766-2006 deem some individuals residents and others not; not in the source
--       bundle, so the rule declines where the caller says they reach the individual.
-- s 14(b) displaces the definition for a first-time resident's adjustment year; outside this row,
-- and declined where it reaches.
--
-- So the rule answers TRUE or FALSE where a finding has been made, TRUE where a presumption arises
-- unrebutted and no finding has been made, and declines otherwise: the absence of a presumption is
-- not a finding that the centre of life is abroad (fork F26).
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Section 1 — "Israeli resident", for an individual`

-- src:143 | ”תושב ישראל“ או ”תושב“ –
-- src:144 | (א) לגבי יחיד – מי שמרכז חייו בישראל; ולענין זה יחולו הוראות אלה:
-- src:145 | (1) לשם קביעת מקום מרכז חייו של יחיד, יובאו בחשבון מכלול קשריו המשפחתיים, הכלכליים והחברתיים, ובהם בין השאר:
-- src:146 | (א) מקום ביתו הקבוע;
-- src:147 | (ב) מקום המגורים שלו ושל בני משפחתו;
-- src:148 | (ג) מקום עיסוקו הרגיל או הקבוע או מקום העסקתו הקבוע;
-- src:149 | (ד) מקום האינטרסים הכלכליים הפעילים והמהותיים שלו;
-- src:150 | (ה) מקום פעילותו בארגונים, באיגודים או במוסדות שונים;
-- src:151 | (2) חזקה היא שמרכז חייו של יחיד בשנת המס הוא בישראל –
-- src:152 | (א) אם שהה בישראל בשנת המס 183 ימים או יותר;
-- src:153 | (ב) אם שהה בישראל בשנת המס 30 ימים או יותר, וסך כל תקופת שהייתו בישראל בשנת המס ובשנתיים שקדמו לה הוא 425 ימים או יותר;
-- src:154 | לענין פסקה זו, ”יום“ – לרבות חלק מיום;
-- src:155 | (3) החזקה שבפסקה (2) ניתנת לסתירה הן על ידי היחיד והן על ידי פקיד השומה;
-- src:156 | (4) שר האוצר, באישור ועדת הכספים של הכנסת, רשאי לקבוע תנאים ולפיהם יראו יחיד שאינו תושב ישראל לפי פסקאות (1) ו־(2) כתושב ישראל, ובלבד שהתקיים בו אחד מאלה:
-- src:157 | (א) הוא עובד מדינת ישראל;
-- src:158 | (ב) הוא עובד רשות מקומית בישראל;
-- src:159 | (ג) הוא עובד הסוכנות היהודית בארץ ישראל;
-- src:160 | (ד) הוא עובד הקרן הקיימת לישראל, קרן היסוד – המגבית המאוחדת לישראל;
-- src:161 | (ה) הוא עובד חברה ממשלתית;
-- src:162 | (ו) הוא עובד רשות ממלכתית או תאגיד שהוקם לפי חוק, וכן רשאי הוא לקבוע כאמור כי סוגי יחידים שרואים אותם כתושבי ישראל לפי פסקאות (1) או (2), לא יראו אותם ככאלה, והכל בתנאים שיקבע;
-- src:163 | [note: פורסמו תקנות מס הכנסה (קביעת יחידים שיראו אותם כתושבי ישראל וקביעת יחידים שלא יראו אותם כתושבי ישראל), התשס״ו–2006.]

@ref ITO s 1, "תושב ישראל" (a)(2), lines 151-154
GIVEN y IS AN `An individual's year, for the definition of Israeli resident`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 1 "Israeli resident" (a)(2) — a presumption that the centre of life is in Israel arises, for` y MEANS
        y's `days in Israel in the tax year` AT LEAST 183                                              -- (a)
    OR  (    y's `days in Israel in the tax year` AT LEAST 30
         AND y's `days in Israel in the tax year and the two tax years before it` AT LEAST 425)        -- (b)

@ref ITO s 1, "תושב ישראל" (a)(4), line 156; regulations of 5766-2006, line 163, not in the source bundle
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the regulations under paragraph (4) of the definition of Israeli resident are not encoded in this model` MEANS
    REFUSE "the regulations under paragraph (4) of the definition of Israeli resident are not encoded in this model"

@ref ITO s 14(b), line 1141 — outside this row
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 14(b) displaces the definition of Israeli resident, and is not encoded in this model` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 14(b) displaces the definition of Israeli resident, and is not encoded in this model"

@ref ITO s 1, "תושב ישראל" (a)(1), (3), lines 145-150, 155
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`no finding of the centre of life has been made, and no unrebutted presumption decides it` MEANS
    REFUSE "no finding of the centre of life has been made, and no unrebutted presumption decides it"

-- The definition of "Israeli resident" alone. Version 0.2.0: it does not see the second limb of the
-- definition of "foreign resident" (below), which turns on other tax years than the one asked about;
-- for an individual that limb may reach, the form below declines. The independent tests call this
-- form with the record alone, so it is kept.
@ref ITO s 1, "תושב ישראל" (a), lines 143-163
GIVEN y IS AN `An individual's year, for the definition of Israeli resident`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 1 "Israeli resident" (a) — an Israeli resident in the tax year:` y MEANS
    `for tax year` (y's `tax year`) `, row IL-08 answers`
        (BRANCH
            IF   y's `regulations made under paragraph (4) reach the individual`
            THEN `the regulations under paragraph (4) of the definition of Israeli resident are not encoded in this model`
            IF   y's `section 14(b) reaches the individual in the tax year`
            THEN `section 14(b) displaces the definition of Israeli resident, and is not encoded in this model`
            OTHERWISE
                CONSIDER y's `the centre of life, as found on the whole of the individual's ties`
                WHEN JUST `where` THEN `where` EQUALS `in Israel`
                WHEN NOTHING THEN
                    IF   `s 1 "Israeli resident" (a)(2) — a presumption that the centre of life is in Israel arises, for` y
                         AND NOT y's `the presumption has been rebutted`
                    THEN TRUE
                    ELSE `no finding of the centre of life has been made, and no unrebutted presumption decides it`)

§§ `Section 1 — the second limb of "foreign resident" (version 0.2.0, D019)`

-- "תושב חוץ" is one who is not an Israeli resident, AND an individual who meets both limbs below, his
-- centre of life notwithstanding:
-- src:167 | ”תושב חוץ“ – מי שאינו תושב ישראל, וכן יחיד שהתקיימו בו כל אלה:
-- src:168 | (א) הוא שהה מחוץ לישראל 183 ימים לפחות, בכל שנה, בשנת המס ובשנת המס שלאחריה;
-- src:169 | (ב) מרכז חייו לא היה בישראל, כאמור בפסקה (א)(1) להגדרה ”תושב ישראל“ או ”תושב“, בשתי שנות המס שלאחר שנות המס האמורות בפסקת משנה (א);
-- Version 0.1.0 had no coverage row for this definition and answered "resident" on a centre-of-life
-- finding whatever the later years held (the independent pass's D019). The text does not say for
-- which tax year the limb deems the individual a foreign resident (the first of the pair, or both),
-- nor whether the deeming prevails over a centre of life in Israel in that year (fork F34). So where
-- the first definition makes him an Israeli resident in the tax year, and the limb is met for a pair
-- of tax years that includes it (the year before and this one, or this one and the next), the rule
-- declines; and where the facts given do not settle whether it is met, it declines for want of them.
-- Where the first definition makes him not resident, the limb only agrees, and the answer stands.

DECLARE `What the facts given show of the second limb of "foreign resident", for a pair of tax years` IS ONE OF
    `the limb is met`
    `the limb is not met`
    `the facts given do not settle it`

-- The facts given for one tax year (none, if the year is not in the list).
GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
      `years`    IS A LIST OF `A tax year of the individual, for the second limb of "foreign resident"`
GIVETH A LIST OF `A tax year of the individual, for the second limb of "foreign resident"`
`s 1 "foreign resident" — the facts given for tax year` `the year` `, among` `years` MEANS
    filter (GIVEN r YIELD r's `tax year` EQUALS `the year`) `years`

-- (a) for the pair beginning in tax year P (P and P + 1); (b) for the two tax years after them
-- (P + 2 and P + 3). Met where every one of the four facts is given and holds; not met where any is
-- given and fails.
@ref ITO s 1, "תושב חוץ", second limb, lines 167-169
GIVEN `the first year` IS A NUMBER
      `years`          IS A LIST OF `A tax year of the individual, for the second limb of "foreign resident"`
GIVETH A `What the facts given show of the second limb of "foreign resident", for a pair of tax years`
`s 1 "foreign resident", second limb — for the pair of tax years beginning` `the first year` `, on the facts` `years` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF       any (GIVEN r YIELD NOT r's `outside Israel 183 days or more in the tax year`) (`facts of` `the first year`)
             OR  any (GIVEN r YIELD NOT r's `outside Israel 183 days or more in the tax year`) (`facts of` (`the first year` PLUS 1))
             OR  any (GIVEN r YIELD NOT r's `the centre of life was not in Israel in the tax year`) (`facts of` (`the first year` PLUS 2))
             OR  any (GIVEN r YIELD NOT r's `the centre of life was not in Israel in the tax year`) (`facts of` (`the first year` PLUS 3))
        THEN `the limb is not met`
        IF       any (GIVEN r YIELD r's `outside Israel 183 days or more in the tax year`) (`facts of` `the first year`)
             AND any (GIVEN r YIELD r's `outside Israel 183 days or more in the tax year`) (`facts of` (`the first year` PLUS 1))
             AND any (GIVEN r YIELD r's `the centre of life was not in Israel in the tax year`) (`facts of` (`the first year` PLUS 2))
             AND any (GIVEN r YIELD r's `the centre of life was not in Israel in the tax year`) (`facts of` (`the first year` PLUS 3))
        THEN `the limb is met`
        OTHERWISE `the facts given do not settle it`
    WHERE
        `facts of` q MEANS `s 1 "foreign resident" — the facts given for tax year` q `, among` `years`

@ref ITO s 1, "תושב חוץ", second limb, lines 167-169: fork F34
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the second limb of the definition of foreign resident is met for a pair of tax years that includes this one, and the text says neither which tax year it deems nor whether it prevails over a centre of life in Israel` MEANS
    REFUSE "the second limb of the definition of foreign resident is met for a pair of tax years that includes this one, and the text says neither which tax year it deems nor whether it prevails over a centre of life in Israel"

@ref ITO s 1, "תושב חוץ", second limb, lines 167-169
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the second limb of the definition of foreign resident turns on the days outside Israel and the centre of life in the neighbouring tax years, and the facts given do not settle it` MEANS
    REFUSE "the second limb of the definition of foreign resident turns on the days outside Israel and the centre of life in the neighbouring tax years, and the facts given do not settle it"

@export Whether an individual was an Israeli resident in a tax year from 2024 under Income Tax Ordinance s 1 ("Israeli resident" (a)), from a recorded finding of the centre of life or, where none was made, the day-count presumptions of paragraph (2); declines a resident whom the second limb of "foreign resident" reaches, or may reach on the facts given
@ref ITO s 1, "תושב ישראל" (a), lines 143-163; "תושב חוץ", lines 167-169
GIVEN y       IS AN `An individual's year, for the definition of Israeli resident`
          @desc the tax year, the days in Israel in it and in the two years before (part of a day counts), any finding of where the centre of life is, whether a presumption was rebutted, and whether the 2006 regulations or s 14(b) reach the individual
      `years` IS A LIST OF `A tax year of the individual, for the second limb of "foreign resident"`
          @desc for each tax year from the year before to the third year after whose facts are known: whether the individual was outside Israel 183 days or more in it, and whether his centre of life was not in Israel in it; a year not known is left out
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 1 — an Israeli resident in the tax year, the second limb of "foreign resident" considered:` y `, the neighbouring tax years being` `years` MEANS
    IF   NOT `s 1 "Israeli resident" (a) — an Israeli resident in the tax year:` y
    THEN FALSE
    ELSE BRANCH
             IF   `the pair before` EQUALS `the limb is met` OR `the pair from this year` EQUALS `the limb is met`
             THEN `the second limb of the definition of foreign resident is met for a pair of tax years that includes this one, and the text says neither which tax year it deems nor whether it prevails over a centre of life in Israel`
             IF   `the pair before` EQUALS `the facts given do not settle it` OR `the pair from this year` EQUALS `the facts given do not settle it`
             THEN `the second limb of the definition of foreign resident turns on the days outside Israel and the centre of life in the neighbouring tax years, and the facts given do not settle it`
             OTHERWISE TRUE
    WHERE
        `the pair before`        MEANS `s 1 "foreign resident", second limb — for the pair of tax years beginning` (y's `tax year` MINUS 1) `, on the facts` `years`
        `the pair from this year` MEANS `s 1 "foreign resident", second limb — for the pair of tax years beginning` (y's `tax year`) `, on the facts` `years`
